Author: Tormod Haugland <tormod.haugland@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 9 07:20:52 2026 +0100

    Hold W3 clients through a hived handover and adopt Apiary-written service units (deploy design D5): RpcClient.connect (the hive CLI and the daemon client apiaryd consumes through the library) treats a connect failure while runtime/handover.json beside the daemon's data dir is younger than 60 s as a wait (retry every 100 ms) instead of DaemonDownError, fails typed HandoverStalledError (hived_handover_stalled, with the marker and its age) once the marker is older, and without a marker retries a refused connect once because the successor removes the marker right after it listens; the marker helpers move to v2/daemon/src/handoverMarker.ts so the thin client does not import the runtime-update service; a socket closed before the server hello is a connect failure at once instead of a 3 s timeout. RpcServer.close stops accepting first (the socket path is unlinked, so new connects get ENOENT and hold on the marker), drains in-flight requests (quiet 150 ms, 1 s cap) and only then destroys connections, so a send accepted by the old daemon is answered rather than cut. hive daemon install adopts the runtime the node runs: the unit's explicit entry (the form Apiary's updater writes, ExecStart naming ~/.apiary/honeybee-runtime/<hash>/lib/node_modules/honeybee/dist/cli.js), else an external runtime/current link, else the CLI's own entry when current is absent, is copied into runtime/<sha> by retainExternalCurrent (clean honeybee build identity for this target, verbatim symlinks, containment check, tree digest before and after, rename under runtime/.deploy.lock; same bytes already installed is quiet, different bytes install_conflict), current is retargeted to it, the launcher is written and ExecStart goes through launch and current with the old unit's interpreter as the node pin. Deleted: the explicit-entry unit form (serviceExecArgs returns only the launcher form, service_runtime_missing typed when runtime/current has no dist/cli.js) and the HIVE_V2_SERVICE_ARGS override with their tests. The verify-runtime-handover model gains one client, the marker's age and a stalling service manager: a send across the swap is never duplicated, its outcome is true and known, a refusal with a fresh marker is a wait, the hold is decided only on a fresh marker, the stall failure is typed; four new broken variants fail. Proven on a scratch node with a fake service manager (.proof/D5, next commit): an Apiary-written unit is adopted (bytes copied, current retargeted, ExecStart through the launcher, one daemon-reload), 18 sends started inside a 1.8 s window with no socket all land exactly once alongside a library send, the pre-D5 CLI fast-fails in the same window, a send 2 s into a stalled handover fails hived_handover_stalled at marker age 60 s and one 61 s in fails at once, and the recovered successor serves.
    
